Jan 28, 2026:
    Initial version 1.0 release

Feb 20, 2026:
    Version 1.1 release.
    Added version numbers to save file headers.
    Added VEV32 preprocessor symbol & real typedef
	for selecting 32 bit vev's and poly coeffs.

Feb 9, 2026:
    Added Version.h.
    Added VEV32 preprocessor symbol & real typedef for selecting 32 bit vev's
    and poly coeffs.
    Added version numbers to save file headers, incompatibility checking in
    Save::read_header.

Feb 27, 20206:
    Added PAGESIZE preprocessor definitions in Save.cpp, used in I/O buffer
    alignas specifications.
    Enclosed std::locale("en_US.UTF-8") statements in Print.cpp in try/catch block.

Mar 1, 2026:
    Added Parse::eos to encapuslate proper testing for end of input string.

Mar 7, 2026:
    Fixed definition of is_coord() in Obs.h

Apr 11, 2026: Version 1.2.
    Fixed Version::arith and added Version::rsize.
    Removed installation of even-length fermion generators in Gen::geninit.
    Changed autoEgens to autoToddgens, and added Op::flipT to auto-create
	T-odd fermion generators from T-even generator definitions.
    Added Numerics::tikhanov to allow adjustment of Lagrange matrix regularization.

Apr 14, 2026:
    Modified Coupling.{h,cpp} and Theory.cpp to allow products of powers of adjustable
    coupling constants as coefficients in Hamiltonian (or free energy) terms.
    Modified Makefile with commend about possible definition of MASSSCALE symbol.

May 24, 2026:
    Version 1.3 release.
    Fixed bogus Gauss law use in 1D Efermion canonicalizations.
    Changed spectrum eigensystem to use smaller second order form.
    Removed Numerics::tikhanov shift as not useful.
    Added 'active' boolean to Gen's.
    Added generator add, suspend & activate commands.
    Deprecated previous "add generator" command.
    Support use for Eigen library instead of Armadillo for linear algebra,
	intended just for testing with 80-bit precision on Intel processors.
    Fixed Global::stageinit and related routines so that observable lists and
	polynomials scripts are not unnecessarily cleared upon a change of stage.

June 16, 2026:
    Version 1.4 release.
    Revamped initialization routines to disentangle initialization and generator
	definition from minimization stage. Changes include creating the OpList class
	and splitting Op::list into separate gauge and fermion OpList's held in
	global.stageinfo.ops.
    Moved nobsG and nobsF members from Global into associated ObsList.
    Ensure that Obs::catalog does not store into a frozen list.
    Added "stage" member to Coupling class, and made setting of coupling value
	automatically switch to associated minimization stage.
    Fixed initial setting of fermion maxord to 1 in obsinit, else GAxf misclassified.
    Fixed critical error affecting fermions additions to Canon::cache.

June 20, 2026:
    Minor code cleanup: merged conversion of printable characters into Symb's
    into the SymbStr(string&) constructor, eliminating to_symb(string&).
    Make ObsList internals private, but expose const_iterator.
    Moved global defs from Init.cpp into inline defs in appropriate .h files.

July 10-24, 2026:
    Version 1.5 release.
    Changed SymbStr -> Str throughout for consistency with master field program delphi.
    Build.cpp: Added mk_ham, called at conclusion of mk_obs, to store
	canonicalized form of H (or F) in cpoly entries of global.info().Hterms.
    Coupling.h: Added Coupling::ncoupG item to track number of gauge couplings.
    Coupling.cpp: Added Coupling::values to return comma separated list of
	coupling values (used for output MMA files).
    Data.h: Added HamHdr struct and associated functions for ham record.
	Changed DataRec constructor to require SysIndex ref.
    Global.h: Moved SysIndex into stage specific StageInfo entry.
	Moved all output path & stream items to stage specific StageInfo entries.
	Moved ObsList::nobs[GF] to StageInfo nobs.
	Added StageInfo::obshash to hold Obs list checksums.
	Added SerialData constructor taking SysIndex ref.
	Added ham entry to Serial Data for hamiltonian/free energy.
	Added PolyArr constructor taking SysIndex ref.
    Global.cpp: Renamed dfltfilename to mk_filename and reworked to
	construct standard YM* and QCD* file names.
	Added stageabbrev for constructing part of standard file names.
	Added addsubdir for creating & appending theory specific subdirs.
    Init.cpp: Moved definitions of global and ObsList's into Init.cpp
	to ensure proper ordering of initializations depending on global.
    Numerics.cpp: Improved error message for unbuilt geodesic equations.
    Obs.cpp: Fixed test in ObsList::catalog for attempt to catalog into frozen list.
	Added code to ObsList::store to update obshash and nobs entries
	in global.info() upon addition to ObsList::obs.
	Added ObsList::rehash, ObsList::hasher and changed ObsList::purge
	to update obshash entries in global.info.
    Parse.cpp: Removed "set sysfile" and "set vevfile" commands.
	Added parsing of "load <coupling> <value>" command.
    Poly.h: Added public & private constructors for PolyArr to pass
	SysIndex ref to non-default DataRec constructor.
    Poly.cpp: Added ObsPoly::add to convert Poly to ObsPoly.
    Print.cpp: Added ObsList hash values to stats report.
	Merged print_hamiltonian and print_freeenergy into print_ham_or_free.
    Save.h: Added Obs list hash codes to FileHdr, with consistency testing
	added in Save::read_header.
    Save.cpp: Reworked Save::save_sys, save_vev and load_save to fully separate
	gauge information in YM* files and fermi information in QCD* files.
	Added write_ham and read_ham to include canonicalized form of hamiltonian
	(or free energy) in save files.
	Removed all support for user-provided save files names.
	Added test to prevent rewriting sys-info file with swapped-out geodesics.
    Theory.cpp: Removed initialization of canonicalized forms of H or F, to
	await construction of ObsList::obs.

July 26, 2026:
    Version 2.0 release.
    Changed packed polynomial encoding to be more efficient: numerous changes
	to Poly.{h,cpp}, Save.{h,cpp}, Build.cpp, Print.cpp, Data.h.
	Note that sys-info files are not backwards compatible.
    Removed redundant "add gen" command.
    Gordion.h: introduced NUM32 typedef to select 32-bit integers and floats
	for polynomial indices and coefficients, with default now being
	64-bit indicies and coefficients.

